Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:05:45.00,Demo,,0,0,0,,ILLUSTRATIVE DEMO  |  Small-dataset model assumption
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.00,0:00:07.40,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Operational overview
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.00,0:00:07.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,FloodGuard AI: an actual browser walkthrough. Models are assumed trained on small datasets; all demonstrated readings are illustrative.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.40,0:00:15.72,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Command statistics
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.40,0:00:15.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,National screening summarizes district risk, priorities, and monitoring intervals in one command view.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:15.72,0:00:26.82,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Command statistics
Dialogue: 1,0:00:15.72,0:00:26.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,The river summary compares city discharge and forecast values, with timestamps and a manual refresh control.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:26.82,0:00:37.92,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Command statistics
Dialogue: 1,0:00:26.82,0:00:37.92,Caption,,0,0,0,,The rainfall table compares current, recent, and forecast rainfall across the four operational cities.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:37.92,0:00:49.02,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Command statistics
Dialogue: 1,0:00:37.92,0:00:49.02,Caption,,0,0,0,,System information shows the configured data mode, monitoring interval, and active risk engine.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.02,0:01:00.12,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  National GIS layers
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.02,0:01:00.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,Toggle district boundaries, screening, waterways, catchments, and monitoring categories on the interactive map.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.12,0:01:11.22,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Reference outlines and Flood Hub integration
Dialogue: 1,0:01:00.12,0:01:11.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,Compare the available Kashmir outlines and enable Flood Hub markers. The gauges shown here are illustrative integration examples.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:11.22,0:01:22.32,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Coordinate lookup
Dialogue: 1,0:01:11.22,0:01:22.32,Caption,,0,0,0,,Enter latitude and longitude to inspect local coverage. The selected coordinate is pinned on the map.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:22.32,0:01:33.42,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Catchment study mode
Dialogue: 1,0:01:22.32,0:01:33.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,Enable corresponding layers to focus on the selected district and hydrological sub-basin, including matching river features.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:33.42,0:01:44.52,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Station hover cards
Dialogue: 1,0:01:33.42,0:01:44.52,Caption,,0,0,0,,Hover and pin a priority monitoring station to inspect readings, provenance, and stored trends.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.52,0:01:55.62,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Station discharge forecast
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.52,0:01:55.62,Caption,,0,0,0,,Station details link to an interactive forecast, separate historical series, date inspection, a readings table, and CSV download.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:55.62,0:02:06.72,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Glaciers and headwaters
Dialogue: 1,0:01:55.62,0:02:06.72,Caption,,0,0,0,,Inspect glacier coverage and upstream drainage, including glaciers that contribute to Pakistan's river basins.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:06.72,0:02:17.82,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Satellite water extent
Dialogue: 1,0:02:06.72,0:02:17.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,Select a place to display a dated satellite water-mask overlay. This recording uses an illustrative U-Net output.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:17.82,0:02:28.91,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Rainfall heatmap
Dialogue: 1,0:02:17.82,0:02:28.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,Switch between observed accumulation windows and 24-hour or 72-hour forecasts. Colors follow the rainfall scale.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:28.91,0:02:40.01,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Population exposure analysis
Dialogue: 1,0:02:28.91,0:02:40.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,GIS Operations estimates exposed people and mapped settlements, with district or tehsil breakdowns and coverage information.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:40.01,0:02:51.11,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Exposure controls and map overlays
Dialogue: 1,0:02:40.01,0:02:51.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,The analysis supports historical water, configured segmentation, uploaded polygons, and synthetic scenarios; inspect the existing result and its\Nlayers.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:51.11,0:03:02.21,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Predictive model views
Dialogue: 1,0:02:51.11,0:03:02.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,Five predictive views cover riverine, flash, urban, seasonal basin, and upstream or transboundary risk, with forecast times and target selectors.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.21,0:03:09.61,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Riverine short-term model
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.21,0:03:09.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,Riverine forecasts: XGBoost baseline inputs, Trimmu and Balloki targets, discharge forecasts, and flood classes over 24–48 hours.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:09.61,0:03:17.01,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Flash-flood model
Dialogue: 1,0:03:09.61,0:03:17.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Flash-flood guidance combines rainfall, soil moisture, and GIS features for catchment risk within six hours.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:17.01,0:03:28.11,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Urban flooding model
Dialogue: 1,0:03:17.01,0:03:28.11,Caption,,0,0,0,,Urban susceptibility uses city-scale targets, rainfall, drainage context, and selectable forecast intervals.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.11,0:03:35.51,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Seasonal basin model
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.11,0:03:35.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,Seasonal basin risk shows forecasts over weeks to months, with target-specific risk series.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:35.51,0:03:42.91,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Upstream anomaly model
Dialogue: 1,0:03:35.51,0:03:42.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,Upstream and transboundary risk highlights anomalous flow changes over hours to days. Model outputs are illustrative in this demo.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.91,0:03:54.01,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Upstream source flood watch
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.91,0:03:54.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Select upper-basin stations, compare GloFAS and GEOGloWS series, and inspect historical trends, rainfall, and forecast risk signals.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.01,0:04:01.41,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Source forecast context
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.01,0:04:01.41,Caption,,0,0,0,,Each station includes provider summaries, expected peaks, rainfall context, location details, and scheduled or manual refresh.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:01.41,0:04:12.51,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  River monitoring table
Dialogue: 1,0:04:01.41,0:04:12.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,Filter monitoring stations by river or name, switch units, and compare current flow, forecasts, flood categories, and expected peaks.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.51,0:04:19.91,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Station network and chart
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.51,0:04:19.91,Caption,,0,0,0,,Open a station to inspect its upstream network and forecast. Chart legends and date inspection help distinguish the displayed series.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:19.91,0:04:31.01,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Citizen reports
Dialogue: 1,0:04:19.91,0:04:31.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,Citizen reports provide a scrollable database-backed feed, coordinates, optional image or video links, priority flags, and closure status.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:31.01,0:04:42.10,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Submit a geolocated report
Dialogue: 1,0:04:31.01,0:04:42.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,Create a report using coordinates, browser location, or a Google Maps link. Image GPS fields remain visible when no geotag is available.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.10,0:04:52.28,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Prioritize and close reports
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.10,0:04:52.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,Flag a report for attention, then close it in the database. New reports appear in the active window before remaining in the saved feed.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:52.28,0:05:03.38,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Monitoring simulation
Dialogue: 1,0:04:52.28,0:05:03.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,Configure a station, measurement, units, test thresholds, and a reading profile to exercise the monitoring workflow.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:03.38,0:05:10.78,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Threshold crossing and saved results
Dialogue: 1,0:05:03.38,0:05:10.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,Play the test scenario. Threshold crossings save simulated readings and create linked alerts and incidents.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:10.78,0:05:18.18,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Alert review
Dialogue: 1,0:05:10.78,0:05:18.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,Review threshold alerts, distinguish operational and simulated flows, and open the linked incident.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:18.18,0:05:26.50,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Incident management
Dialogue: 1,0:05:18.18,0:05:26.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,The incident view records severity, status, location, and timestamps. Linked details preserve the simulated-flow context.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:26.50,0:05:33.90,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  System activity
Dialogue: 1,0:05:26.50,0:05:33.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,The activity timeline records model decisions, monitoring changes, report actions, and simulated response events.
Dialogue: 1,0:05:33.90,0:05:45.00,Chapter,,0,0,0,,FLOODGUARD AI  /  Command overview
Dialogue: 1,0:05:33.90,0:05:45.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,The walkthrough covers the portal as it runs in a web browser. Small-dataset training is an assumption; this video does not validate model\Naccuracy.
